<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61868" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαμπ-τήρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆρος</span>,
			ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάμπω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stand</i> or
			<i>grate</i> for pine and other wood used <i>for lighting
			rooms</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.307
			</span></i> sq., <i><span class="en">
				343
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				19.63
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ χαῖρε, λ. νυκτός</span>
			<i>thou that lightest up</i> the night, of a beacon-fire, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				22
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕσπεροι λαμπτῆρες</span> the
			evening <i>watch-fires</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				286
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡλίου λαμπτῆρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					60
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> epith. of
			Dionysus, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				7.27.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>lantern</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				34
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Int.</u>
				26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				5.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aen.Tact.
				22.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCornell</u>
				1.85
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. ἀντιπεφραγμένος</span>, of a
				horn-<i>lantern</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philist.
				15
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				84.3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. μὴ ἔχοντι τὸ κύκλῳ δέρμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					531a5
				</span></i>
			.</div>
